---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Bias Mirror — Your writing, turned into a mirror">
  <section class="py-10 text-center">
    <h1 class="serif-h text-4xl font-bold text-charcoal">Your writing, turned into a mirror.</h1>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-charcoal">
      Upload journals, notes, or drafts. Bias Mirror surfaces the cognitive
      patterns hiding in your own words — with quoted evidence for every flag.
    </p>
    <a
      href="/upload"
      class="mt-6 inline-block rounded bg-rust px-6 py-3 font-bold text-cream"
    >
      Upload writing
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 rounded border border-sand bg-white p-6">
    <h2 class="serif-h text-2xl text-charcoal">Redacted example</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-70">A flagged passage looks like this:</p>
    <blockquote class="mt-4 border-l-4 border-rust bg-cream px-4 py-3 italic">
      “I <span class="bg-sand px-1 font-bold not-italic text-rust">always knew</span> the launch would fail —
      <span class="bg-charcoal px-1 not-italic text-cream">██████</span> agreed with me from the start.”
    </blockquote>
    <div class="mt-3 flex gap-2 text-xs">
      <span class="rounded bg-sand px-2 py-1 font-bold text-rust">confirmation bias · 0.72</span>
      <span class="rounded bg-sand px-2 py-1 font-bold text-rust">in-group bias · 0.61</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 text-sm text-charcoal opacity-80">
    <h2 class="serif-h text-xl text-charcoal opacity-100">A probabilistic note</h2>
    <p class="mt-2">
      Flags are probabilistic suggestions, not diagnoses. The detector matches
      language patterns against 15 known biases and quotes the sentence that
      triggered each flag — always read the evidence and decide for yourself.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
